Expected elements: present

Every must-show is there and no must-not-show is. The focused control is the identity bar's `.dbgid[data-copy]` at x85-194; the truncated value is fully legible; the `Data` row carries `Synthetic demo data`; `← demo` exits to the chain; `FETCHING` is live. Panes verified byte-clean.

MEASURED, AND IT IS THE HEADLINE. Against `debugger--link-exact__wide__light` (same route, plain build) this image differs by **568 pixels, all of them the focus outline at x81-197, y17-45**. Below y=62: zero differing pixels in 1,955,200. No layout shift, no `.copied`, no banner — and nothing else drawn either. §13's "true one-click copy button arrives with hydration" is HALF-KEPT: the capability arrives, the button does not.

The ring is NOT a UA default — measured `#3b82f6` light / `#60a5fa` dark, 2px, identical bbox; that is `--bt-focus-ring` via `styles.nim:114`'s `[tabindex]:focus-visible`. The shared primitive reaches the new control and survives dark. The gap is entirely the RESTING state: `.copybtn` is unstyled, so at rest the control joins none of this register's three drawn primitives (`.dcbtn`, `.dcbtn.off`/`.btn.disabled`, `.copyable`). Outside the vocabulary, not adjacent to it. A sighted keyboard user sees a rectangle meaning "focused"; the AT layer hears `button, "Copy 0xb636167a…"`. The two accounts disagree.

Keep the promise, do not withdraw it. Fixes: (1) give `.copybtn` `.copyable`'s own treatment — `cursor:copy`, `--bt-radius-xs`, hover surface + hairline — which also stops the ring being the bar's only square rectangle; (2) draw `.copied`/`.copyfailed` (Q23 c).

Three false claims in the expectation block, filed against the instrument.

Rating: 7/10

